[b]Futures Context Module[/b] is a Daily-only context dashboard for the futures information a CFD or spot chart cannot provide on its own: Open Interest, ΔOI, and the front/next term structure of an explicitly configured futures contract pair.

[b]What it does[/b]

It reads Open Interest and the front-month/next-month term structure directly from a futures contract pair you configure — never comparing the chart symbol's own price against the futures price. The front/next spread is two legs of the same futures feed, so it stays internally consistent regardless of what instrument the chart itself is showing.

[b]Data shown[/b]

[list]
[*]Open Interest for the front contract, with a visible "no OI feed" state instead of a silent zero
[*]ΔOI read against the front contract's own price change, classified into new longs / new shorts / short covering / long liquidation
[*]Front/Next term structure: Contango / Backwardation / Flat, plus a curve-trend read
[*]Real-volume validity check on the front contract (base/quote volume only — tick volume is flagged, not used)
[/list]

[b]Configuration[/b]

Front-Month and Next-Month futures symbols are set explicitly via two symbol inputs — there is no automatic guessing from the chart symbol. An unconfigured or misconfigured pair, or a symbol with no data feed, shows a visible status instead of a blank table. The module only computes on Daily and higher timeframes; intraday charts show a notice instead.

[b]What it is not[/b]

This is a context display, not a signal generator. There are no entries, no alerts, and no comparison between the chart price and the futures price.

